The F1 rows were captured on `c25a149`. The only later commit, `d32f7b7`, changes `tasks.md` and the evidence files, so those rows carry over unchanged.

The F1 matrix had no row for regressions in neighbouring behaviour, which the skill requires, so I added QA6. On the real CLI, totals of a million or more print a separator in the wrong place: `big,1234567.89` prints `1234,567.89` and `big,12345678.90` prints `12345,678.90`. On `main` these printed `1234567.89`. The broken `groupThousands` regex inserts one comma, before the last three digits only.

**Wave recorded:** `GC wave --outcome qa=FAIL --blocker QA6` returned `DECISION: CONTINUE`, with one fix round left at `standard` depth.

**Fix round 1 (row 4.1), commit `20fb5fb`:**
- `groupThousands` now uses `/\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g`, so it separates every group of three digits.
- A regression test expects `1,234,567.89` and `12,345,678.90`. It failed on the old code (it received `1234,567.89`) and passes now. Full suite: 5 pass, 0 fail.
- Row 4.1 is added under a new `## 4. F2 fixes` group in `tasks.md`. Both the `--plan-only` validator and `validate-openspec-change` still pass.
- The delta patch and manifest are at `.omp/team-config/gate-deltas/F2-4.1-20fb5fb8e973-20261102205824/`.

